# The chemotion_ELN source the integration suite was last run green against, as a p2d build
# (p2d.sh, README.md "Testing against an unreleased ELN"). When this file exists, `p2d.sh build`
# and `p2d.sh test` called without a ref use it; an explicit ref on the command line still wins.
# Delete the file to fall back to the old default (`main`, unpinned).
#
# Set at least one of the three. p2d.sh fills in the empty ones from the remote and writes them
# back here (a branch or tag only when its tip is exactly that commit; otherwise it stays empty):
#   ELN_COMMIT  full 40-character sha — if set, this is what gets built, so a moving branch
#               cannot change the server under the suite
#   ELN_TAG     a tag; built if no commit is set
#   ELN_BRANCH  a branch; built (its current tip) if neither commit nor tag is set
# The branch (else the tag) names the image: chemotion-eln-p2d:<name>-<short sha>.
# Bump the values together, after a green run against the new commit.
#
# Tested 2026-11-06: main @ a8b47c7 (reports v4.0.0, labimotion 2.3.4).
ELN_BRANCH=main
ELN_TAG=
ELN_COMMIT=a8b47c7d2c0d5c7dd032ada868af45c391d26f1f
